Five NYC restaurants that never miss for date night. A mix of Middle Eastern, Korean, and Caribbean, which happen to be my three favorite cuisines.

Cuerno (Midtown). Northern Mexican steakhouse with incredible carnes and service that actually pays attention.

@casincharlie (LES). Korean tapas with Southern influence. Very good, very affordable.

Shukette (Chelsea). Some bomb ass food. Just order everything off the menu.

@ilili Restaurants (NoMad). My favorite Lebanese spot in the city.

Kabawa

@bynainyc A cozy, intimate lounge that’s perfect for conversation. I especially loved it for a business meeting, relaxed enough to sit and chat without having to commit to a full meal. During the day, it has a quiet, comfortable atmosphere that would work just as beautifully for catching up with someone or enjoying a more intimate afternoon with your partner. ♥️

I visited during the daytime, so I can’t speak to the evening atmosphere just yet.

